<mxCell id="n173" value="&lt;b style=&quot;color:#b85450;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:1px&quot;&gt;HOW IT CONNECTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11px;color:#3a3a34;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;ethercat_driver&amp;#x27;s EthercatDriver implements SystemInterface; its read()/write() exchange PDO process-images with the EtherLab IgH master each cycle. Per joint an EcCiA402Drive module runs the CiA 402 state machine and maps SI↔raw via a source-controlled YAML (factors, offsets, SDO init). The two ankles aren&amp;#x27;t direct-drive: harambe_ankle_ethercat_driver (v1 analytic / v2 calibrated-cubic) wraps the driver and converts joint pitch/roll ↔ the two pushrod motors with IK/FK + Jacobian.&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbfbf7;strokeColor=#b85450;fontColor=#3a3a34;dashed=0;arcSize=3;strokeWidth=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=4;spacingLeft=9;spacingRight=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1716" y="2722" width="1628" height="86" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
